{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Disposition — re-typed `bug` -> `story`, claim released, left OPEN for a dedicated implementer\n\nNot abandoned. The RCA comment above is the current, runtime-proven analysis and is the right\nstarting point for whoever picks this up.\n\n### Why this is not a bug\n\nThe mechanism is proven and the gap is real: `before_model_request` DOES fire before the first\nrequest and DOES receive the outgoing wire, so the seam is **not** misplaced — the filter is.\n`proc(messages)` only descends into `ModelResponse` + `_is_failed_output_response`, and a first\nrequest's history is `[ModelRequest]`, so the sole raise site is unreachable. Measured: 3,604,182\nchars went out against a 1,000,000-token window with `_wire_keeps_response` invoked **0 times**.\nThe guard's silence is not a \"fits\" verdict — it never executed.\n\nBut per the not-a-bug guard, a proven mechanism is not by itself a defect. No authority\nestablishes this seam was MEANT to guard the first request:\n\n- Design ticket `66b3-4214-c70b-4a9a` scopes the rule to \"**that response's own**\n  `usage.input_tokens + output_tokens`\". No AC names the first or outgoing request, and its\n  held-out oracle can only trigger the overflow by scripting a *response*.\n- The sibling fix five days ago (`0076113ee8`) explicitly considered extending this seam and\n  **deliberately declined**, choosing the op-local posture.\n- Stated fairly, one authority points the other way: `errors.py:43-48` describes the error's\n  trigger in request terms (\"system/user/tool content\"), which is genuinely broader than the\n  implementation's reachability. That argues the guard **under-delivers**, not that the repair is\n  small.\n\n### Why it cannot be done as a bug fix — three required additions, all widening\n\n1. **No measurement exists to filter to.** The current check never measures message content; it\n   reads `response.usage.input_tokens`, the provider's already-billed count from the PREVIOUS\n   turn. A `ModelRequest` has no usage. A first-request check needs a new local token estimator.\n2. **The estimator's calibration is load-bearing, and the codebase disagrees with itself by 2x.**\n   `enrich`/`completion_criteria` use chars/2; `det_floor` and two inline lambdas use chars/4.\n   `enrich` bounds its source to `window * 2` **chars** — a chars/2 seam estimator scores that at\n   exactly `window`, and `window + reserve > window` fails closed, **breaking this ticket's own\n   AC#3**. chars/4 passes. Picking the constant decides whether an op keeps working.\n3. **The posture question is open by this ticket's own admission** — its Scope section defers\n   \"decide the posture per op class\" and \"should per-op bounds defer to the shared seam\" to\n   whoever claims it.\n\n### What the next implementer must answer, in order\n\n1. **Calibration** — one shared constant, chosen so `enrich`'s `window * 2`-char bound stays\n   admissible.\n2. **Posture** — fail-closed at the seam, or catchable per op.\n3. **Convergence** — whether the four per-op bounds defer to the shared seam or stay local.\n\n### Blast radius (measured)\n\n15 modules reach this seam. `ContextWindowExceededError` has zero consumers outside the module\nand its oracle. The type swap itself is contained — both it and today's `LLMUnavailableError` are\n`LLMError`, caught by the 13 broad handlers. **The real risk is calls that succeed today being\nnewly refused by a conservative estimator**, which is why calibration comes first.\n\n### Split out as its own bug\n\nThe complementary defect — a `CHANGE_INPUT` 400 surfacing as `LLMUnavailableError`\n(provider-outage semantics) for a deterministic, caller-fixable input problem — needs no\nestimator, no calibration, and no new measurement. Filed separately and linked. It does NOT\nsatisfy AC#1 (\"before the provider call\"), so it is a complement, not a substitute.\n\n### Attribution retained\n\n`caused_by -> 66b3-4214-c70b-4a9a` (`012aef629c`, 2026-08-16), an **omission**, never a\nregression: `git log -L 176,220` returns exactly one commit and the file is new in it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787311890394985001,"uuid":"61ec5f4b-9686-4009-b5cd-5f96ef0163c8"}